<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea buys 322,400T of grains, oilseeds in July.</title>
<headline>S.Korea buys 322,400T of grains, oilseeds in July.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea bought at least 322,400 tonnes  of grains and oilseeds during July through tenders and private negotiations,  traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>The total broke down into 187,000 tonnes of corn, 43,500 tonnes of  U.S. wheat, 40,000 tonns of U.S. soybean, 30,000 tonnes of Brazilian  soymeal, 11,500 tonnes of Indian rapeseed meal, and 10,400 tonnes  of palm kernel meal.</p>
<p>This compared with a total of 536,800 tonnes purchased in June.</p>
